e1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"The legacy OS and kernel were preserved, and a persistent, effective yum exclusion held curl/libcurl across a verified reboot. The main contract is only partially proven because the update attempt encountered no enabled repositories and therefore did not exercise the hold during an actual package transaction. The provider-wide restart protocol was completed coherently: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered node, package, configuration, and service state were all observed and agree with the fixed lifecycle snapshots.","limitations":["No enabled repositories were available, so the evidence does not directly show curl remaining fixed during a system update that updates other packages or offers a newer curl version.","The lifecycle package-health probe timed out both before and after execution; targeted rpm verification was clean, but a complete package-manager consistency comparison is unavailable.","The retained /tmp/yum.conf.before-curl-hold file is minor executor-created residue."]}
